#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119610 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119799 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7634b3ac-f9e6-514e-87ba-e78590c9fa53" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 Linear System Using LU Factorization"}] :question/id #uuid "9552ad30-9d46-5884-9877-18ca8842c252" :question/math-academy-id "e-4775" :question/problem "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $\\mathbf{b},$ given by\n![](images/f1/f1124e83e3b7614557a1a6de54523cc99f62ba2a52af1da8e4d22e14466ce020.svg)\nIf $\\langle x_1,x_2 \\rangle$ and $\\langle y_1,y_2 \\rangle$ are the solutions to the systems $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ and $L\\mathbf{y}=\\mathbf{b}$ respectively, what is the value of $x_1 \\cdot y_2?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $U\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{y},$ we obtain\n\n![](images/a1/a185a6fd91c78ed3e291b3ac8b99f9430290e5d8c1060a7d97317efc230aeb40.svg)\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $L\\mathbf{y} = \\mathbf{b}.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n![](images/1e/1e780d384ca1fd957d742bbd047399c558ab016d187ce4cf71682546673aba35.svg)\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=6 \\\\ -2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} &=-8.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is $y_1=6$ and $y_2=4.$ Therefore, \n![](images/58/58da62903247cf6dfdf33be86293c181ef5184048ca7cd6c921360e5d202f353.svg)\n\n- Next, we solve $U\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{y}.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n![](images/e0/e0563dde4944ecbe2ccb98bc91246fa18c7a808df96ab77f9f8efb5510084677.svg)\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}7{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} &=6 \\\\ -2{x}_{2} &=4.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is $x_2=-2$ and $x_1=2.$ Therefore, \n![](images/a8/a84088cff2a3589652ef7cabf09e3d8429fad7797ea20d44a416f85dcc7f9b65.svg)\n\nFinally, $x_1 \\cdot y_2 = 2 \\cdot 4 = 8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119611 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119800 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9fa9fbb8-b2bc-5c93-bb07-bc8c7ef7c115" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "24bc4954-462b-5066-83d4-8a4a87efc7b7" :question/math-academy-id "e-4777" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $\\mathbf b,$ given by \n![](images/a1/a13a7752a224bdabc27558a6a41e2b24d3c7918af1ca4d9cff802dcb54259238.svg)\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $\\mathbf{y}$ such that\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $U\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{y},$ we obtain\n\n![](images/60/605f569e0b4a54d2ca68d7b3330a2a0ebb06dcaba2b7efa911f58dbffd796fb0.svg)\n\nWe now solve $L\\mathbf{y} = \\mathbf{b}.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n![](images/d2/d259a6740aa32e0e577756375fd85589b815232314511c74dc434a88d0146a3b.svg)\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=2 \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2} &=4 \\\\ {y}_{1}-2{y}_{2}+{y}_{3} &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =2, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =4-{y}_{1} \\\\  & =4-(2) \\\\  & =2, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =1-{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2} \\\\  & =1-(2)+2(2) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n![](images/c5/c5198aa83d3976d992b200f63941261f952282fedb241db780c20c12c97e3ba9.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119706 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119886 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5250e0e1-4909-5075-8a8e-aa2f1be0bd9a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "cbefba9a-eda2-5a8e-8bb5-59ea4175b835" :question/math-academy-id "e-8926" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $\\mathbf b,$ given by \n\n![](images/9d/9d0b186213211813b290f502888f68e0603bc9f77bcd7ea9d6262cb7449c00e7.svg)\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $\\mathbf{y}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $U\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{y},$ we obtain\n\n![](images/42/4298fe244fd6c66c7623ad508c97b96464321387506aa1e4be5e2399a5c9a862.svg)\n\nWe now solve $L\\mathbf{y} = \\mathbf{b}.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 15 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 66\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=5 \\\\ 15{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} &=66.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is $y_1=5$ and $y_2=-9.$ \n\nTherefore, ![](images/a8/a86dfd0e07b8c415e526764cf9f7ba8f020609bf7b13cc90536deba868ec4aa6.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479145 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119886 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5250e0e1-4909-5075-8a8e-aa2f1be0bd9a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c72a1a6-e9cc-5dc7-8129-ca02b99a9f47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 11\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478603} {:answer/id #uuid "204b0962-b138-56df-b0fd-2796efaabbe5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 50\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478609} {:answer/id #uuid "81b0d9a3-f05e-52aa-baca-6aa189c65731" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ 49\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478756} {:answer/id #uuid "9043cde5-3c71-5771-9a3d-347775e2a488" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -49\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478790} {:answer/id #uuid "fa9afe1b-bb2b-5925-8cb5-cfde20011076" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ 39\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478950}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9043cde5-3c71-5771-9a3d-347775e2a488" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -49\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478790} :answer-field/id #uuid "db587132-2223-5d73-bd8b-93dbc82d6d91" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479043}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fb1f16a0-3031-5b97-a1fa-27b860c24df9" :question/math-academy-id "q-105753" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 11 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 50\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 11 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 50\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=9 \\\\ 11{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} &=50.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=9$ and ${y}_{2}=-49.$ \n\nTherefore, $y=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -49\\end{bmatrix}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479106 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119886 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5250e0e1-4909-5075-8a8e-aa2f1be0bd9a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0043e87e-f842-57e6-82bc-b4ea7ec5f162" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 50\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478563} {:answer/id #uuid "2e8f7d3a-59d4-56b1-9c28-1128e20099aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -78\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478632} {:answer/id #uuid "4856545f-c7b8-5207-946b-42bd4c1c3aa8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 64\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478660} {:answer/id #uuid "92afe7cc-d13c-59a1-b5db-5b37ab35d121" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ -50\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478798} {:answer/id #uuid "f363ef1a-e780-507a-81d1-0ea4237f7e39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 60\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478939}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0043e87e-f842-57e6-82bc-b4ea7ec5f162" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 50\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478563} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b6940e4-bb59-563a-a937-e93f48ec1bc6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478972}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "88def0e2-16e4-59a7-96bb-d850c4ea1c49" :question/math-academy-id "q-105758" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -8 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -14\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -14\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=8 \\\\ -8{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} &=-14.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=8$ and ${y}_{2}=50.$ \n\nTherefore, $y=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 50\\end{bmatrix}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241124 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119886 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5250e0e1-4909-5075-8a8e-aa2f1be0bd9a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d4b3937-d636-543e-b0d6-739f7a00e7f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 34\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238719} {:answer/id #uuid "59c3bb80-7b1c-535e-843c-7be8777981fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ -34\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238826} {:answer/id #uuid "d6a16e65-a824-55dd-90aa-570d8ce9e4fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 24\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239931} {:answer/id #uuid "dbc1e9dc-6f28-50f2-90f2-765e57d990e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 36\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239972} {:answer/id #uuid "ec701eb0-1499-57d0-9f0b-83cacf08003b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -36\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240133}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d4b3937-d636-543e-b0d6-739f7a00e7f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 34\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238719} :answer-field/id #uuid "06e2738a-d273-5c9d-8b63-8b44a8f24c45" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240338}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d3a99bb0-e72d-5183-bc18-0817eb820005" :question/math-academy-id "q-105760" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -36\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -36\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=7 \\\\ -10{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} &=-36.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=7$ and ${y}_{2}=34.$ \n\nTherefore, $y=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 34\\end{bmatrix}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241144 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119800 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9fa9fbb8-b2bc-5c93-bb07-bc8c7ef7c115" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3721f084-e142-5f33-baa4-f1483ad8f031" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 16 \\\\ -23\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238533} {:answer/id #uuid "7792733b-cca3-5632-a467-f04ba2ce6d0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239087} {:answer/id #uuid "7e797d6d-322e-55f6-9562-6057b788f863" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239155} {:answer/id #uuid "a4a111c4-fc76-59c9-ae42-fc127091245d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -11\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239483} {:answer/id #uuid "e1791bdd-9f67-5cb2-8e6c-a0895f1b851c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -11\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240034}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3721f084-e142-5f33-baa4-f1483ad8f031" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 16 \\\\ -23\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238533} :answer-field/id #uuid "1267ab7e-a947-5495-96a5-cfc2042f7e77" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240358}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f817b0d9-deca-51e1-aedb-860b4e44d9bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-105930" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=-2 \\\\ 9{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} &=-2 \\\\ -4{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}+{y}_{3} &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =-2, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =-2-9{y}_{1} \\\\  & =-2-9(-2) \\\\  & =16, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =1+4{y}_{1}-{y}_{2} \\\\  & =1+4(-2)-(16) \\\\  & =-23.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$y=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 16 \\\\ -23\\end{bmatrix}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241145 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119800 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9fa9fbb8-b2bc-5c93-bb07-bc8c7ef7c115" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "253c5bec-a5e7-5fe4-8936-ee84f06ad2cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ 70 \\\\ 80\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238380} {:answer/id #uuid "3431ca67-1154-5315-a55d-30d8b6ec10fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -63 \\\\ 81\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238506} {:answer/id #uuid "5467b34d-2f1e-5c78-85dd-2b5382f7e7be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -56 \\\\ 80\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238782} {:answer/id #uuid "b152e191-5d18-598f-a23e-0286d0d7f786" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ 56 \\\\ -80\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239602} {:answer/id #uuid "c8674c02-d35b-548c-9f92-7fdac92d42e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -70 \\\\ 80\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239819}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5467b34d-2f1e-5c78-85dd-2b5382f7e7be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -56 \\\\ 80\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238782} :answer-field/id #uuid "697b8f6f-9b78-510a-bdce-c0f202963523" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240524}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "90586eea-75b4-50dc-8971-26e34a9a2816" :question/math-academy-id "q-105934" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=9 \\\\ 7{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} &=7 \\\\ -9{y}_{1}+{y}_{3} &=-1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =9, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =7-7{y}_{1} \\\\  & =7-7(9) \\\\  & =-56, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =-1+9{y}_{1} \\\\  & =-1+9(9) \\\\  & =80.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$y=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -56 \\\\ 80\\end{bmatrix}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241146 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119799 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7634b3ac-f9e6-514e-87ba-e78590c9fa53" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 Linear System Using LU Factorization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16cfc4d9-e678-5d11-a711-f03b27d03ba7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238251} {:answer/id #uuid "48196e4d-5923-5fc3-ba09-551bba37a5f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238683} {:answer/id #uuid "764a88ed-d42b-5e8e-b7e6-0154d79ebcb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239076} {:answer/id #uuid "9c69f59a-92c5-5712-8d12-87a782265e35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239415} {:answer/id #uuid "a7a8dd22-491e-5bf2-8293-73bb146e224b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7a8dd22-491e-5bf2-8293-73bb146e224b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239509} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0090a32-0dee-5d9f-b495-d9dbbf4db605" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240613}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b76bf109-a8c3-51c0-a007-3381911cc6e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-105951" :question/problem "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $b,$ given by\n\n$$\nA={{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{L}{{\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{U},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 20\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $⟨{x}_{1},{x}_{2}⟩$ and $⟨{y}_{1},{y}_{2}⟩$ are the solutions to the systems $Ax=b$ and $Ly=b$ respectively, what is the value of ${x}_{2}\\cdot {y}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=b=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 20\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=6 \\\\ 4{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} &=20.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=6$ and ${y}_{2}=-4.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\ny=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n- Next, we solve $Ux=y.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=y=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=6 \\\\ 4{x}_{2} &=-4.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${x}_{2}=-1$ and ${x}_{1}=\\frac{5}{2}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{2}\\cdot {y}_{2}=(-1)\\cdot (-4)=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479056 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119886 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5250e0e1-4909-5075-8a8e-aa2f1be0bd9a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24c66c0e-e0d0-5c27-907f-9e31b4c17877" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478616} {:answer/id #uuid "44df3446-722a-5a1f-9400-f9c2edb4a1ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478656} {:answer/id #uuid "a1b54213-3d59-59c8-98ef-a8f08dbb4c4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478822} {:answer/id #uuid "d1de89e0-2dc2-5990-94a4-6e3067c9a319" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478892} {:answer/id #uuid "e65b36d6-4ce8-57b8-a24e-fa7877ec664c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478916}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e65b36d6-4ce8-57b8-a24e-fa7877ec664c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478916} :answer-field/id #uuid "61c0b255-63a0-5164-9dd6-3298c1d228e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478996}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "084c02e4-7974-5581-92ae-668d0f97c0f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-107170" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=2 \\\\ -3{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} &=-2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=2$ and ${y}_{2}=4.$ \n\nTherefore, $y=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244037 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119886 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5250e0e1-4909-5075-8a8e-aa2f1be0bd9a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "427af4b2-096b-5dbf-8f00-52882f2904b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 33\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241778} {:answer/id #uuid "565699cb-5aa4-56e7-8959-bd5585b64c79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241960} {:answer/id #uuid "9561d87e-a040-5eb9-9f47-8c4ea9835a94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242492} {:answer/id #uuid "b51413cc-3563-5af6-ac17-74e0247a8a5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242763} {:answer/id #uuid "cf0370c3-16bd-5ef9-95a0-be7a53155a4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "427af4b2-096b-5dbf-8f00-52882f2904b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 33\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241778} :answer-field/id #uuid "029bf18c-8249-5883-8d70-894701f6abe7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243440}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d9df65e2-b577-593b-b89c-fc5d55ad0bf6" :question/math-academy-id "q-107171" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=5 \\\\ -7{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} &=-2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=5$ and ${y}_{2}=33.$ \n\nTherefore, $y=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 33\\end{bmatrix}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558529 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119800 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9fa9fbb8-b2bc-5c93-bb07-bc8c7ef7c115" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14beea86-f47c-5a8c-9bec-dff707ad6098" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557916} {:answer/id #uuid "2e855c15-8cb8-5eb3-ad1a-06b9a164a41f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557963} {:answer/id #uuid "9cb700b3-de35-5eef-a9b9-8f936285f7aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558175} {:answer/id #uuid "9dd0b1f6-0564-5713-91c8-8b44037f4570" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558178} {:answer/id #uuid "a2fda1e6-ea2c-5685-8e6d-c69133ac2877" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558189}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9dd0b1f6-0564-5713-91c8-8b44037f4570" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558178} :answer-field/id #uuid "72d3d84a-5d38-5708-8891-cf429ce55b84" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558415}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "772e6d55-2cc0-5849-b50b-b1451b60fe6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-107185" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -5 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -5 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=-1 \\\\ -2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-3 \\\\ 8{y}_{1}-5{y}_{2}+{y}_{3}=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =-1, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =-3+2{y}_{1} \\\\  & =-3+2(-1) \\\\  & =-5, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =8-8{y}_{1}+5{y}_{2} \\\\  & =8-8(-1)+5(-5) \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$y=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558571 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119799 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7634b3ac-f9e6-514e-87ba-e78590c9fa53" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 Linear System Using LU Factorization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ea7e0be-9a1f-5523-b787-ed5f453051d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557964} {:answer/id #uuid "30c57b85-780d-5e2f-88d6-2b0bf8507810" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557967} {:answer/id #uuid "6b2c83f9-30fa-58a9-ab6d-b815a4faa3cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558075} {:answer/id #uuid "978ea838-5cf8-51dc-9cc3-827714cd57ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558160} {:answer/id #uuid "fad0f84d-6ada-5fb9-b0e6-bd2a4abb6d9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ea7e0be-9a1f-5523-b787-ed5f453051d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557964} :answer-field/id #uuid "97da889e-de7b-5fe7-9f12-0a62150c1338" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558433}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e26325a0-a17c-5d3b-96e5-ffcb13cdecc2" :question/math-academy-id "q-107491" :question/problem "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $b,$ given by\n\n$$\nA={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U},\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $⟨{x}_{1},{x}_{2}⟩$ and $⟨{y}_{1},{y}_{2}⟩$ are the solutions to the systems $Ax=b$ and $Ly=b$ respectively, what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {y}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=b=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=-3 \\\\ 3{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=-3$ and ${y}_{2}=2.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\ny=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Next, we solve $Ux=y.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=y=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${x}_{2}=1$ and ${x}_{1}=-1.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {y}_{2}=(-1)\\cdot 2=-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558528 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119799 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7634b3ac-f9e6-514e-87ba-e78590c9fa53" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 Linear System Using LU Factorization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13c02160-8ba1-5939-bc73-8002657c6b03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557912} {:answer/id #uuid "23f077b2-98bc-5e17-b96a-87b4b7d0879e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557942} {:answer/id #uuid "6de90c59-9c12-5214-92b7-f0abb8a7ca70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558082} {:answer/id #uuid "cadf1f12-7d08-5b35-add1-a8807ac05198" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558272} {:answer/id #uuid "fade0afc-801b-5fae-b3a9-b016601c272f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558358}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fade0afc-801b-5fae-b3a9-b016601c272f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558358} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4f155d4-3ea5-53d0-a6f6-8b69b1f92207" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558468}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "758b84b6-7328-584d-83ee-1df88702770d" :question/math-academy-id "q-107500" :question/problem "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $b,$ given by\n\n$$\nA={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}8 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U},\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $⟨{x}_{1},{x}_{2}⟩$ and $⟨{y}_{1},{y}_{2}⟩$ are the solutions to the systems $Ax=b$ and $Ly=b$ respectively, what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{y}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=b=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=4 \\\\ -{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=4$ and ${y}_{2}=5.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\ny=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Next, we solve $Ux=y.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}8 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=y=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}8{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ {x}_{2}=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${x}_{2}=5$ and ${x}_{1}=3.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{y}_{2}=3+5=8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377100 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119800 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9fa9fbb8-b2bc-5c93-bb07-bc8c7ef7c115" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "122c6d88-8494-5aec-a026-229428468b5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377102} {:answer/id #uuid "a24fc545-7e28-5319-b8ea-0050a0425013" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377103} {:answer/id #uuid "565b9eb2-7221-52ec-8a34-db861601dd2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377104} {:answer/id #uuid "66cde035-3c2e-5045-8a57-e62cdfc4c320" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377105} {:answer/id #uuid "5ec426d5-6612-5ded-909b-99d6a4c1702f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377106}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66cde035-3c2e-5045-8a57-e62cdfc4c320" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377105} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa4faae0-0911-57b4-a7e3-89f58f84a03e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377101}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bf45deeb-ab83-510b-8f67-2f8280e43963" :question/math-academy-id "q-32543" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=1 \\\\ -2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} &=-2 \\\\ -{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}+{y}_{3} &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =1, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =-2+2{y}_{1} \\\\  & =-2+2(1) \\\\  & =0, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =2+{y}_{1}-{y}_{2} \\\\  & =2+(1)-(0) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$y=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390757 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119799 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7634b3ac-f9e6-514e-87ba-e78590c9fa53" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 Linear System Using LU Factorization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "032457e9-02bf-5ad6-9987-99a0689c6243" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390759} {:answer/id #uuid "ad2b9196-139c-5abe-8bf3-f21b13bb615e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390760} {:answer/id #uuid "d6722917-7648-59db-8da1-966d52f9d9ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390761} {:answer/id #uuid "9541c84f-6c02-5508-afe7-624da511dbdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390762} {:answer/id #uuid "749e40df-d35d-5ad6-9d4a-9737f8552554" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390763}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad2b9196-139c-5abe-8bf3-f21b13bb615e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390760} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e79de7e-b384-5ea6-bb81-dfd5832cccb2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390758}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b44ae0d1-f2bc-52f5-a02c-1e4fb0c1d4e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-32561" :question/problem "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $b,$ given by\n\n$$\nA={{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{L}{{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{U},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $⟨{x}_{1},{x}_{2}⟩$ and $⟨{y}_{1},{y}_{2}⟩$ are the solutions to the systems $Ax=b$ and $Ly=b$ respectively, what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {y}_{1}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=b=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=3 \\\\ -2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} &=-3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=3$ and ${y}_{2}=3.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\ny=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n- Next, we solve $Ux=y.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=y=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} &=3 \\\\ 2{x}_{2} &=3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${x}_{2}=\\frac{3}{2}$ and ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{3}{2}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {y}_{1}=-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot 3=-\\frac{9}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558501 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119799 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7634b3ac-f9e6-514e-87ba-e78590c9fa53" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 Linear System Using LU Factorization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53492803-619c-5738-8780-eb85ef78082a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558022} {:answer/id #uuid "5b75e368-dcfe-5035-a89a-0de98b0c81f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558040} {:answer/id #uuid "641e7890-d858-55b5-b90c-31018a57894b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558059} {:answer/id #uuid "9acf41c5-2aee-5e2e-9787-52e0c514e5e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558168} {:answer/id #uuid "b4885fca-3afa-5082-a83c-7abaa4f102b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558224}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53492803-619c-5738-8780-eb85ef78082a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558022} :answer-field/id #uuid "791205e6-0e35-509a-8763-c44c2a7914e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558418}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2b4d31f2-6228-5e16-8ece-d3de14298eac" :question/math-academy-id "q-32563" :question/problem "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $b,$ given by\n\n$$\nA={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U},\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $⟨{x}_{1},{x}_{2}⟩$ and $⟨{y}_{1},{y}_{2}⟩$ are the solutions to the systems $Ax=b$ and $Ly=b$ respectively, what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {y}_{1}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=b=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=-4 \\\\ -{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=-4$ and ${y}_{2}=-5.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\ny=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- Next, we solve $Ux=y.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=y=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-4 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${x}_{2}=-\\frac{5}{2}$ and ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{3}{2}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {y}_{1}=(-\\frac{3}{2})\\cdot (-4)=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479090 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119800 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9fa9fbb8-b2bc-5c93-bb07-bc8c7ef7c115" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "067598d2-ade2-5dd5-8073-c389ff24174b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478568} {:answer/id #uuid "1c178bab-1c92-5a25-ae64-df6277ac397a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478602} {:answer/id #uuid "3aea1048-26e5-56d0-bd6c-955510f59840" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478642} {:answer/id #uuid "81992826-cc58-58c1-a7a5-01d46348c63f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478755} {:answer/id #uuid "a28f92ee-2682-564b-832c-3e2a4ecbc8c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478826}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a28f92ee-2682-564b-832c-3e2a4ecbc8c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478826} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d96da9c-3e97-52fd-92c9-c73ab85d4165" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479021}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "53971d39-ffaa-5c20-9081-d54743d61b0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-32579" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=6 \\\\ -{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} &=-2 \\\\ {y}_{1}-{y}_{2}+{y}_{3} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =6, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =-2+{y}_{1} \\\\  & =-2+6 \\\\  & =4, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =-{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} \\\\  & =-(6)+4 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$y=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.$"}]}
